# Task 8: one compute path, and a preflight that stays cheap

## Context

This is where "the Lakeflow job is the only compute path" becomes true in the
code rather than just in the design. The `mode` argument, the `store` parameter,
`max_triples` and `allow_pushdown_fallback` are gone from
`compute_graph_metrics` and `run_metrics_task`, and so is the fallback Task 6
left behind: a failed job run used to answer with SQL-pushdown numbers, which is
the worst possible outcome — the user sees plausible figures computed by a
different algorithm and has no way to tell. A failed run now raises.

The review of the first pass caught two problems with the new snapshot probe.
It ran from the stats payload, which renders on every page, so every uncached
page view paid a SQL round-trip that can take tens of seconds against a cold
warehouse. And it swallowed every exception into "the table is missing or empty.
Run Build", sending someone off to rebuild a domain when the real cause was a
sleeping warehouse or a permissions gap. Both are fixed below.

## Changes

1. `src/back/objects/digitaltwin/DigitalTwin.py` — `compute_graph_metrics` and
   `run_metrics_task` lost `store`, `mode`, `max_triples`,
   `max_nodes_betweenness` and `allow_pushdown_fallback`. The pushdown fallback
   is deleted; the method is now resolve-source → build → compute, and any
   failure propagates.
2. `src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py` — Split the preflight in two.
   `_analytics_job_configured` is the three checks that cost nothing (toggle, job
   name, resolvable snapshot) and is what the stats payload calls;
   `_analytics_job_status` adds the warehouse probe and is called only where a job
   run is about to be launched. `_data_table_has_rows` now returns `None` when the
   probe itself failed, which produces a "retry in a moment" reason instead of
   blaming the Build, and logs at WARNING so an operator can see it. The
   `POST /metrics/compute` endpoint lost its mode selection and oversized branch;
   the stats payload lost `analytics_max_triples` and
   `analytics_pushdown_available`.
3. `tests/units/dtwin/test_analytics_job_status.py` — Added the unreachable-probe
   case (must not say "Build"), and two tests pinning that the cheap check never
   probes and that the stats endpoint is the caller using it.
4. `tests/units/dtwin/test_dtwin_analytics.py`, `tests/units/api/test_dtwin_analytics.py`
   — Tests that a failed job run propagates rather than degrading, and that the
   source table is wired through to the runner.

## Modified Files

- `src/back/objects/digitaltwin/DigitalTwin.py`
- `src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py`
- `tests/units/dtwin/test_analytics_job_status.py`
- `tests/units/dtwin/test_dtwin_analytics.py`
- `tests/units/api/test_dtwin_analytics.py` (new)

## Test Result

`pytest -q -m "not scenario"` → **3809 passed, 275 skipped, 0 failed**

