# Tasks 9 and 10: delete the dead paths, then make the UI stop describing them

## Context

With every metric computed by the Lakeflow job, `GraphMetrics` (NetworkX) and
`PushdownMetrics` (engine SQL) were two complete metric implementations no code
path could reach — the kind of thing that gets accidentally revived or silently
diverges from the job's definition of the same number. They are gone, along with
`MODE_IN_MEMORY`, `MODE_PUSHDOWN` and `Settings.analytics_pushdown_enabled`.

The UI was then the last place still telling the user a story that was no longer
true: a banner about in-memory size caps, a field the stats payload no longer
sends, and — worst — a message saying betweenness could not be computed and to
"pick an Entity Type above to analyse a subgraph in memory", an instruction that
had become impossible to follow. The settings help text was equally stale: it
claimed Lakebase `app_managed` and Neo4j were unsupported and that a missing
prerequisite "degrades to engine-side aggregation instead of failing". Both
statements were the opposite of the truth after Tasks 5 and 8.

Deleting the two test modules also silently dropped the only coverage of
`profiles.py`, which survives and is now the only analytics computation left in
the app. Pinning it directly turned up a pre-existing false positive in
`has_temporal_predicates`, recorded as a strict xfail rather than changed —
fixing it alters what the UI reports for existing domains, so it is a decision
rather than a cleanup.

## Changes

1. `src/back/core/graph_analysis/` — `GraphMetrics.py` and `PushdownMetrics.py`
   deleted, with `supports_pushdown` and the two mode constants; `models.py` now
   defaults `MetricsResult.mode` to `MODE_JOB` and notes why a single-valued
   constant still exists.
2. `src/shared/config/settings.py`, `app.yaml.template` —
   `analytics_pushdown_enabled` removed. `analytics_max_triples` stays; cluster
   detection still uses it.
3. `tests/units/core/test_profiles.py` — New file covering `local_name`,
   `has_temporal_predicates` and `flat_reasons` directly, including a strict
   xfail for the short-keyword false positive (`assignedTo` reads as temporal
   because "dt" appears inside it).
4. `src/front/templates/partials/dtwin/_query_analytics.html` — Dropped the
   over-limit banner, the size-cap wording and the removed
   `analytics_pushdown_available` field. Run Analysis is gated on
   `analytics_job_available`; a blocked job shows its specific reason. The
   in-memory escape hatch in the unavailable-metric copy is replaced with the
   remedy that actually exists: raise the job's max depth and re-run.
5. `src/front/templates/settings.html` — Rewrote both help paragraphs for the
   single path: analytics runs only in the job, works identically on every
   backend because it reads the snapshot each Build materialises, and names the
   missing prerequisite instead of falling back.
6. `src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py` — Legacy stored results still render; the
   guarantee is the absence of a mode gate, so the stored dict is spread through
   untouched rather than routed via a no-op helper.
7. `tests/units/settings/test_analytics_job_toggle.py`,
   `tests/units/dtwin/test_analytics_job_status.py` — Help-text assertions
   updated to the true prerequisites, plus one that the copy never promises a
   fallback, and one that the latest-metrics read path never compares a stored
   mode against `MODE_JOB`.

